)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":37.51,"default_fair_val":37.51,"premium_pct":-24.3,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":20.5,"pe_forward":18,"pb_trailing":1.8,"pb_forward":1.6,"div_yield":0.11,"ps_ratio":4.2,"fcf_to_ev":8.18,"fcf_to_mcap":5.89,"liab_to_assets":23.6,"cash_to_assets":37.9,"current_ratio":7.53,"roe":8.6,"roa":6.6,"moat":{"ticker":"SSRM","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"SSRM 屬於黃金開採行業，商品屬性極強，缺乏品牌溢價空間。其產品黃金的價格主要由全球供需及宏觀經濟因素決定，公司本身對價格影響力微乎其微。儘管 SSRM 在生產效率和成本控制上力求卓越，但這更多是運營層面的優勢，而非能轉化為顯著的品牌定價權。與消費品或科技公司不同，黃金礦業公司難以建立消費者忠誠度或品牌認同，因此在品牌定價權維度上得分較低，壁壘極為薄弱。","comment_en":"SSRM operates in the gold mining industry, which is highly commoditized and offers little room for brand premium. The price of its product, gold, is primarily determined by global supply and demand and macroeconomic factors, with minimal influence from the company itself. While SSRM strives for operational efficiency and cost control, these are primarily operational advantages rather than factors that translate into significant pricing power derived from brand strength. Unlike consumer goods or technology companies, gold mining firms struggle to build consumer loyalty or brand recognition, thus scoring low on brand pricing power with extremely weak barriers."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"黃金開採行業的進入壁壘主要體現在礦權的獲取、勘探技術以及環保法規的遵守上。SSRM 作為一家成熟的礦業公司，擁有其運營礦區的合法開採權，這構成了一定的進入門檻。然而，其核心技術並非專利保護的對象，且行業內存在較多競爭者。監管環境雖然嚴格，但並非 SSRM 獨有的特許經營權，其他同業也需遵守。因此，此維度壁壘為中等偏弱，主要依賴於現有礦權的穩定性和合規運營。","comment_en":"Barriers to entry in the gold mining industry primarily lie in acquiring mining rights, exploration technology, and compliance with environmental regulations. As an established mining company, SSRM possesses legal rights to operate its mining areas, which constitutes a certain entry threshold. However, its core technologies are not patent-protected, and the industry has numerous competitors. While the regulatory environment is strict, it does not grant SSRM exclusive operating rights; other industry players must also comply. Therefore, the barrier in this dimension is moderately weak, relying mainly on the stability of existing mining rights and compliant operations."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"SSRM 的客戶主要是黃金的批發買家，如金商、央行或工業用戶。這些客戶在購買黃金時，主要考量的是黃金的純度、重量和即時價格，而非供應商的品牌或服務。轉換供應商的成本極低，客戶可以輕易地從市場上其他礦業公司購買同等質量的黃金。SSRM 難以通過建立客戶忠誠度或提供差異化服務來鎖定客戶，因此在轉換成本維度上幾乎沒有護城河可言。","comment_en":"SSRM's customers are primarily wholesale buyers of gold, such as bullion dealers, central banks, or industrial users. When purchasing gold, these clients focus on purity, weight, and immediate price, rather than the supplier's brand or services. The cost of switching suppliers is extremely low, as clients can easily procure gold of equivalent quality from other mining companies in the market. SSRM finds it difficult to lock in customers by building loyalty or offering differentiated services, thus having virtually no moat in terms of switching costs."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"網絡效應是指產品或服務的價值隨著用戶數量的增加而增加的現象。在黃金開採行業，SSRM 的業務模式與網絡效應幾乎無關。其產品是標準化的商品，銷售對象是批發商，不存在用戶之間互動以提升產品價值的機制。無論有多少客戶購買 SSRM 的黃金，都不會增加其他客戶購買黃金的價值，反之亦然。因此，此維度幾乎不存在任何護城河。","comment_en":"Network effects refer to the phenomenon where the value of a product or service increases with the number of users. In the gold mining industry, SSRM's business model is almost entirely unrelated to network effects. Its product is a standardized commodity sold to wholesalers, and there is no mechanism for user interaction to enhance the product's value. Regardless of how many customers purchase SSRM's gold, it does not increase the value for other customers, and vice versa. Therefore, there are virtually no moats in this dimension."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"SSRM 作為一家大型黃金生產商，在規模經濟方面具有一定的優勢。其較大的產量有助於攤薄固定成本，如設備折舊、勘探費用和管理費用。同時，較大的採購量也能在購買原材料、設備和服務時獲得一定的價格談判能力。然而，黃金開採的成本結構受地質條件、開採難度等因素影響較大，規模效應並非絕對優勢，且行業內仍存在其他規模相當的競爭者。因此，此維度壁壘為堅固的，但非罕見。","comment_en":"As a large-scale gold producer, SSRM possesses certain advantages in economies of scale. Its substantial production volume helps spread fixed costs, such as equipment depreciation, exploration expenses, and administrative overhead. Additionally, larger procurement volumes can provide some pricing negotiation power when purchasing raw materials, equipment, and services. However, the cost structure of gold mining is significantly influenced by geological conditions and mining difficulty, meaning scale advantages are not absolute. Furthermore, other competitors of comparable size exist within the industry. Thus, the barrier in this dimension is robust but not rare."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"SSRM 在特定地理區域擁有重要的礦產資源，例如其在土耳其和南美洲的礦區。這些礦區的品位、儲量以及開採的便利性構成了其獨特的資產壁壘。成功的礦業公司往往需要長期投入來獲取和開發具有經濟價值的礦產地。SSRM 的現有礦權和已探明的儲量，使其在短期內不易被競爭對手模仿或取代。然而，礦產資源的枯竭和新礦的發現具有不確定性，且地理位置的優勢也可能受到地緣政治風險的影響。","comment_en":"SSRM holds significant mineral resources in specific geographic regions, such as its mining areas in Turkey and South America. The grade, reserves, and ease of extraction in these areas constitute its unique asset barrier. Successful mining companies often require long-term investment to acquire and develop economically viable mineral deposits. SSRM's existing mining rights and proven reserves make it difficult for competitors to imitate or replace in the short term. However, the depletion of mineral resources and the discovery of new mines carry uncertainty, and geographical advantages can also be affected by geopolitical risks."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"SSRM 在運營效率方面表現出色，體現在其較低的生產成本和較高的產量。公司持續投資於技術升級和流程優化，以提高採礦效率和降低單位生產成本。其卓越的運營管理能力，能夠在複雜的礦業環境中穩定地產生自由現金流（TTM $341.0M），並維持較高的股本回報率（ROE 8.6%）和資產回報率（ROA 6.6%）。這種持續的效率優勢，使其在行業內具有較強的競爭力，構成了一個堅實的護城河。","comment_en":"SSRM demonstrates excellent operational efficiency, reflected in its relatively low production costs and high output. The company continuously invests in technological upgrades and process optimization to enhance mining efficiency and reduce per-unit production costs. Its superior operational management capabilities enable it to consistently generate free cash flow (TTM $341.0M) in complex mining environments and maintain strong returns on equity (ROE 8.6%) and assets (ROA 6.6%). This sustained efficiency advantage provides it with strong competitiveness within the industry, forming a robust moat."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"SSRM 的財務狀況顯示其擁有充裕的現金儲備（$1,621.0M）和極低的負債（$2.4M），這為其資本配置提供了極大的靈活性。公司能夠通過內生現金流進行再投資、償還債務或進行潛在的股權回購與分紅。其穩健的資產負債表和持續產生自由現金流的能力，表明管理層在資本配置方面採取了相對保守和審慎的策略。儘管黃金行業的資本配置決策受大宗商品價格波動影響，但 SSRM 的財務健康度使其能夠更好地應對市場波動，這構成了一個較強的護城河。","comment_en":"SSRM's financial position indicates substantial cash reserves ($1,621.0M) and extremely low debt ($2.4M), providing significant flexibility for capital allocation. The company can reinvest through internal cash flow, repay debt, or engage in potential share buybacks and dividends. Its sound balance sheet and ability to consistently generate free cash flow suggest management employs a relatively conservative and prudent capital allocation strategy. Although capital allocation decisions in the gold industry are influenced by commodity price volatility, SSRM's financial health allows it to better navigate market fluctuations, forming a strong moat."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"如 M3 轉換成本所述，SSRM 的客戶基礎主要是批發商，他們對供應商的忠誠度極低。黃金作為一種商品，其交易的核心是價格和品質，而非供應商關係。客戶可以輕易地從市場上尋找其他供應商以獲得更優的價格或條件。SSRM 難以通過建立長期的客戶關係或提供差異化的服務來實現高客戶留存率。因此，在客戶留存這一維度上，其護城河極為薄弱。","comment_en":"As mentioned in M3 (Switching Costs), SSRM's customer base primarily consists of wholesale buyers who exhibit extremely low loyalty to suppliers. Gold, as a commodity, is traded based on price and quality, not supplier relationships. Customers can easily find other suppliers in the market offering better prices or terms. SSRM struggles to achieve high customer retention rates by building long-term relationships or providing differentiated services. Consequently, the moat in terms of customer retention is very weak."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"SSRM 的業務模式，即開採和銷售黃金，具有一定的持久性，因為黃金作為貴金屬長期以來一直是價值儲存的手段。只要全球經濟體系存在，對黃金的需求就可能持續存在。然而，礦業的持久性也面臨挑戰，包括礦產資源的枯竭、開採技術的變革、環保法規的日益嚴格以及新興替代資產的競爭。SSRM 的持久性在於其現有礦產資源的壽命和持續發現新礦的能力，這使其在一定程度上具有可持續性，但並非絕對的、不受挑戰的。","comment_en":"SSRM's business model of mining and selling gold possesses a degree of durability, as gold has long been a store of value. As long as the global economic system exists, demand for gold is likely to persist. However, the durability of mining faces challenges, including the depletion of mineral resources, changes in extraction technology, increasingly stringent environmental regulations, and competition from emerging alternative assets. SSRM's durability lies in the lifespan of its existing mineral reserves and its ability to continuously discover new mines, providing a certain level of sustainability, though not absolute or unchallenged."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"SSRM 的經濟護城河整體偏弱，主要依賴於其規模經濟（M5）和獨特的地理礦產資產（M6），以及卓越的運營效率（M7）和穩健的資本配置（M8）。然而，其作為商品型企業，在品牌定價權（M1）、轉換成本（M3）和網絡效應（M4）方面幾乎沒有壁壘，客戶留存率（M9）極低。雖然黃金需求具有長期持久性（M10），但行業競爭激烈且受外部因素影響大。總體而言，SSRM 的護城河更接近於一種「商品型」或「運營型」的優勢，而非巴菲特所青睞的具有強大定價權和客戶黏性的特許經營權。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"SSRM's economic moat is generally weak, primarily relying on its economies of scale (M5) and unique geographical mineral assets (M6), along with excellent operational efficiency (M7) and sound capital allocation (M8). However, as a commodity company, it possesses minimal barriers in brand pricing power (M1), switching costs (M3), and network effects (M4), with extremely low customer retention (M9). While gold demand offers long-term durability (M10), the industry is highly competitive and susceptible to external factors. Overall, SSRM's moat aligns more closely with 'commodity-like' or 'operational' advantages rather than the 'toll bridge' or 'franchise' characteristics with strong pricing power and customer loyalty that Warren Buffett favors.","evidenceHash":"30b484988f5de7266ae2f7c3d3a621338d3d834befb799dc830ad2d9c4b7c432","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"30b484988f5de7266ae2f7c3d3a621338d3d834befb799dc830ad2d9c4b7c432","currentEvidenceHash":"30b484988f5de7266ae2f7c3d3a621338d3d834befb799dc830ad2d9c4b7c432"},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"grey","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T13:46:54.107Z","evidenceHash":"6133104119adf6d6866f0587ba594c99982ca927de45dcc739a4b9d8130a0090"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T13:46:54.107Z","evidenceHash":"6133104119adf6d6866f0587ba594c99982ca927de45dcc739a4b9d8130a0090"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SSRM.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SSRM.png","website":"https://www.ssrmining.com","ceo":"Rodney Antal Accountancy","full_time_employees":"4800","description":"SSR Mining, Inc. is a metals mining company with assets located in four jurisdictions: the USA, Turkiye, Canada, and Argentina, which engages in the operation, acquisition, exploration and development of precious metal resource properties. The firm produces gold ore as well as copper, silver, lead and zinc concentrates. It operates through the following business segments: Copler, Marigold, Crippler Creek and Victor, Seabee and Puna. The company was founded on December 11, 1946 and is headquartered in Denver, CO.","description_en":"SSR Mining, Inc. is a metals mining company with assets located in four jurisdictions: the USA, Turkiye, Canada, and Argentina, which engages in the operation, acquisition, exploration and development of precious metal resource properties. The firm produces gold ore as well as copper, silver, lead and zinc concentrates. It operates through the following business segments: Copler, Marigold, Crippler Creek and Victor, Seabee and Puna. The company was founded on December 11, 1946 and is headquartered in Denver, CO.","description_zh":"SSR Mining Inc.（美股代碼：SSRM）為 Basic Materials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Gold 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"6900 East Layton Avenue","city":"Denver","state":"CO","zip":"80237","country":"US","phone":"303 292 1299","full_address":"6900 East Layton Avenue, Denver, CO 80237, US","range_52w":"19.69-39.44","year_high":39.44,"year_low":19.69,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":19.69,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"BATES THOMAS R JR","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":798,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Booth Brian R","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":798,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Krusi Alan","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":798,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Malchuk Daniel","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":797,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Mullen Laura M","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":798,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Priestly Kay G","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":797,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Swager Karen A","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1668,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Antal Rodney","title":"director, officer: Executive Chairman","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":27018,"price":33.79,"total_val":0.91},{"dat